Embedded React: let a host defer the paint of commits made during JavaScript.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json, in the patch order listed there.
Changed files: engine/include/er_scene.h, engine/scene/compositor.c and
engine/tests/rendering/CMakeLists.txt; new file
engine/tests/rendering/test_deferred_raster.c.
Not proposed upstream: PS5 React maintains this change here.

The reconciler calls NativeUI.commit() after each React commit, and the bridge
runs a full er_commit() for it: layout and a paint. A host that commits once per
frame after the app's JavaScript then paints again for whatever the frame
callbacks advanced. When both touch the same region, as a focus move that
re-renders a row and starts its scroll does, that region is painted twice and
only the second paint reaches the screen.

er_set_raster_deferred(true) makes er_commit() return after layout and layout
events. onLayout handlers therefore still run inside the React commit that
caused them. The dirty flags, vacated footprints and pending scroll moves are
left for the next commit made with deferral off.

test_deferred_raster runs deferred commits that move a box twice, recolour one,
destroy one and scroll a ScrollView in two steps. They must write no pixels and
fire onLayout for each move; the next commit must match a full repaint and
scroll by one copy of the combined offset.

diff --git a/engine/include/er_scene.h b/engine/include/er_scene.h
--- a/engine/include/er_scene.h
+++ b/engine/include/er_scene.h
@@ -1125,6 +1125,19 @@
     void er_commit(void);
 
     /**
+     * @brief Makes er_commit() stop after layout and layout events, leaving the paint to a later commit.
+     *
+     * For a host that commits once per frame after running the app's JavaScript: the reconciler commits
+     * through NativeUI.commit() during that phase, and each of those commits otherwise paints, often the
+     * same region the host's commit then repaints for animations and scrolls the frame advanced. Layout
+     * still runs at each one, so onLayout handlers see the same rects at the same time. Damage carries
+     * over to the next commit made with deferral off.
+     *
+     * @param[in] deferred  true while commits should skip painting; false before the commit that paints.
+     */
+    void er_set_raster_deferred(bool deferred);
+
+    /**
      * @brief Resets the engine to an empty scene: frees every node, clears the root, and resets the
      *        animation, layout-animation, vector, and input subsystems.
      *
diff --git a/engine/scene/compositor.c b/engine/scene/compositor.c
--- a/engine/scene/compositor.c
+++ b/engine/scene/compositor.c
@@ -206,6 +206,8 @@
 static uint16_t s_scroll_pending[ER_SCROLL_PENDING_MAX];
 static uint8_t s_scroll_pending_count = 0U;
 
+static bool s_raster_deferred = false; /**< er_set_raster_deferred(): commits stop after layout. */
+
 /* Layout-dirty gate: er_commit() re-runs the flex + text-measure layout pass only when
  * something that can change a computed rect has happened since the last commit (a prop set,
  * a tree mutation, or a node destroy). Animations mutate render-only props and never set this,
@@ -5691,6 +5693,9 @@
      * are ERUI_MAX_NODES-proportional floors paid even by an idle commit, while composite and blit
      * scale with the damage — the split is what tells a "the pool walk dominates" frame from a "the
      * framebuffer writes dominate" one. */
+    if (s_raster_deferred)
+        return; /* the dirty flags, vacated footprints and pending scrolls wait for the commit that paints */
+
     ER_PERF_BEGIN(ER_PERF_PHASE_RASTER);
     ER_PERF_BLIT_RESET();
     ER_PERF_RASTER_BEGIN(ER_PERF_RASTER_PREPASS);
@@ -6603,6 +6608,11 @@
         data.scroll_y = y;
         h->fn(node, &data, h->user_data);
     }
+}
+
+void er_set_raster_deferred(bool deferred)
+{
+    s_raster_deferred = deferred;
 }
 
 uint32_t er_parallel_frames(void)
